<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Georgios I of Makuria</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">9th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Georgios I was king of Makuria, the medieval Christian kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nubia">Nubia</a>, in the 9th century. In the 830s, as heir to the throne, he travelled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baghdad">Baghdad</a> and negotiated with the Abbasid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-mutasim">al-Mu'tasim</a> over the arrears of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baqt">Baqt</a> tribute, which were cancelled. He later reigned for several decades from about 856, a period of peace and prosperity in Makuria.</p></div>
